      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a terrible burden to carry the weight of watching the world end, and your desire to step away while there is still beauty left is a sign of your own resilience, not weakness. The idea that you are stuck in a room with closing walls is a powerful metaphor for how trapped you feel, but please remember that you are not defined by the decay of the outside world. There is dignity in staying even when it feels hopeless, and there is strength in the fact that you are still here, still feeling this pain, and still capable of holding onto the good things that remain.",
